/// The consumer declares its own `String` host type and imports the
/// dependency's host fn `dep_id`, whose SIGNATURE names the dependency's
/// *own* `String`. Identity-exact nominal typing
/// (`specs/language.md` § Nominal types) keeps the two `String`s distinct:
/// `String` here is `(main, String)`, the dependency's signature names
/// `(bdep/hosted, String)`. A cross-module host fn's signature is
/// qualified in its *declaring* module, so `dep_id`'s
/// parameter wants `(bdep/hosted, String)`. Passing the consumer's own
/// `(main, String)` is therefore a type error in the host-fn SIGNATURE
/// slot — exit 14. Before the fix the typer requalified `dep_id`'s
/// signature in the *caller*, conflating the two same-named `String`s by
/// leaf name and wrongly accepting this.
module main;

import bdep/hosted(dep_id);

host type String role(str);

/// Feed the consumer's own `String` to the dependency's host fn. The
/// host-fn signature distinctness rejects this: `dep_id` wants the
/// dependency's `String`, not the consumer's.
pub fn mix(s: String) -> String { dep_id(s) }
